<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000102> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A disorder that involves some structural damage that is immediately caused by a catastrophic external force." .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000102> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "review target in BBO from disease_terms_review_enriched.csv" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000102> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000102> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "At the scale of organism (as opposed to the cellular scale or the population scale), an injury is typically the result of a catastrophic event. Consider the implications of making 'injury' a subtype of 'disorder'.\n\nNote: Adopted subtype of disorder, and injury can occur at the scale of organism down to cellular level." .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000102> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "injury" .
